{{also|stossen|Stößen}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt-de-ch}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|stōzen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stōzan}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*stautan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stautaną}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro||*stówd-e-ti}}, an o-grade intensive formation from {{m|ine-pro|*(s)tewd-||to hit, push}}.

Akin to {{cog|non|stauta}} and {{m|non|steyta}} (whence {{cog|da|støde}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌿𐍄𐌰𐌽}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{cog|la|tundo}}. Compare {{cog|sa|तुदति|tr=tudáti||to strike, goad}}, {{m|sa|तोद|tr=todá||driver, impeller}}. Related to {{cog|nl|stoten||to push, bump}} and dialectal {{cog|en|stot||to bounce, rebound, ricochet, or make bounce, rebound or ricochet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtoːsən/}}
* {{audio|de|De-stoßen.ogg}}

